Let $Y$ be finite, $r\in(0,1)$, and $s\geq1$ an integer. For every nonempty family $$\mathcal R\subseteq\{T\subseteq Y:1\leq|T|\leq s\}$$ there is a nonempty subfamily $\mathcal Q\subseteq\mathcal R$ with $|\mathcal Q|\leq\lceil2r^{-s}\rceil$ such that $$\label{eq:compression}
 S\text{ satisfies }\mathcal R\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 f_{\mathcal Q}(S)\geq1/2.$$

outputs.exact_statement:
Set $K_0=2^{75}$. For every nonempty finite set $X$, every $r\in(0,1)$, and every family $\mathcal D\subseteq2^X$ with $\mu_r(\mathcal D)\geq1-1/K_0$, the family $$\mathcal E_{K_0}(\mathcal D)=
 \{S\subseteq X:S\not\subseteq D_1\cup\cdots\cup D_{K_0}
                   \text{ for every }D_1,\ldots,D_{K_0}\in\mathcal D\}$$ has a cover of cost at most $1/2$ at the same parameter $r$. The family $\mathcal D$ need not be monotone, and members of a tuple may repeat.

If $H$ has an edge, $|V(H)|\leq n$, and $d=\mathop{\mathrm{degen}}(H)$, then $$\label{eq:q-lower}
 q(H;n)\geq\frac1{2\binom n2},\qquad
 q(H;n)\geq\frac12 n^{-2/d}.$$

Let $Y$ be finite, $r\in(0,1)$, and $s\geq1$ an integer. For every nonempty family $$\mathcal R\subseteq\{T\subseteq Y:1\leq|T|\leq s\}$$ there is a nonempty subfamily $\mathcal Q\subseteq\mathcal R$ with $|\mathcal Q|\leq\lceil2r^{-s}\rceil$ such that $$\label{eq:compression}
 S\text{ satisfies }\mathcal R\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 f_{\mathcal Q}(S)\geq1/2.$$

Let $X$ be a finite set, let $\mathcal F$ be a nonempty family of nonempty subsets of $X$, and suppose that $\mathcal F$ is not $p$-small, where $0<p\le 1$. For each $H\in\mathcal F$, let $\lambda_H$ be a probability mass function on $X$ supported on $H$. Set $D=256$, and let $s\ge 0$ be an integer such that $$p\sum_{i=1}^s D^i\le \frac12.$$ Independently color the elements of $X$ by a map $a:X\to\{1,\ldots,s+1\}$, with color probabilities $$\label{sel:color-probabilities}
  \pi_i=D^ip\quad(1\le i\le s),
  \qquad
  \pi_{s+1}=1-p\sum_{i=1}^sD^i.$$ For a coloring $v$, write $A_i(v)=\{x\in X:v(x)\le i\}$. With probability at least $9/10$, there is an $H\in\mathcal F$ such that $$\label{sel:simultaneous-capture}
  \lambda_H(A_i(a))\ge 1-2^{-i}
  \qquad(1\le i\le s).$$ In particular, with probability at least $9/10$, there is an $H\in\mathcal F$ for which $$\label{sel:average-color}
  \sum_{x\in X}a(x)\lambda_H(x)\le 2.$$

Let $\lambda$ be a probability mass function on a finite set $X$, let $A\subseteq X$, and let $m\ge 0$ and $0<d<1$. Call $u\in[0,1]$ admissible if $$\label{sel:admissible-cutoff}
  \{x:\lambda(x)>u\}\subseteq A,
  \qquad
  \sum_{x\in X}\min\{\lambda(x),u\}
       \bigl(\mathbf 1_A(x)-(1-d)\bigr)\ge mu.$$ If there is an admissible cutoff, there is a largest one, $\varepsilon$, and it satisfies $$|\{x:\lambda(x)>\varepsilon\}|\le \frac{m}{d}.$$
